IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa6-vacancy.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries), the cross-heading "Provisions
-- applying to private companies with a secretary and to public companies": s 274 (lines 3616-3620 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1 of the part agent coa6.
--
-- ss 274A to 279F follow s 274 in this text, each as a heading and a line of dots only (lines 3621-3645, and the omitted
-- cross-heading "..." at line 3633): they are repealed or blank in this text and nothing is encoded for them (NOTES.md,
-- coverage table). The notice "under section 276" that s 272(4)(b) and (5) ask for is therefore a notice under a section
-- this text does not show (finding F-276).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa6-private-and-public.l4. JUST TRUE is the text's yes; JUST FALSE the text's no in its own words
-- (a "where" or "if" condition that fails); NOTHING "not covered". A grant ("may be done by or to") whose "if" gate fails answers
-- NOTHING; one whose "where" gate fails answers JUST FALSE (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Part 12 -- Company secretaries`

§§ `Provisions applying to private companies with a secretary and to public companies`

-- ---- s 274: Discharge of functions where office vacant or secretary unable to act --------------------------------

-- The case the section covers: "Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other
-- reason no secretary capable of acting". It is the text's own "where": outside it the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- src:3618 | Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting, anything required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary may be done—
@ref s 274 Where the office is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting (src:3618)
GIVEN `the office of secretary is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` MEANS
    IF `the office of secretary is vacant` OR `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting"

-- (a): by or to an assistant or deputy secretary (if any). Name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: the gate is the text's "Where" (group (i)),
-- so outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (not flipped); a thing the secretary was not to do or receive, or a person who is not an
-- assistant or deputy secretary, is outside the grant's own wording and stays NOTHING.
-- src:3618 | Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting, anything required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary may be done—
-- src:3619 | (a) by or to an assistant or deputy secretary (if any), or
@ref s 274(a) Anything required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary: an assistant or deputy secretary (src:3618-3619)
GIVEN `the office of secretary is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an assistant or deputy secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 274(a) the thing may be done by or to an assistant or deputy secretary` MEANS
    IF `s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` `the office of secretary is vacant` `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF       `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary`
              AND `the person is an assistant or deputy secretary`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary may be done— (a) by or to an assistant or deputy secretary (if any)"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, group (i), assumed, not ruled): "Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting"; the other reading is NOTHING (F-grants)

-- (b): by or to a person authorised generally or specifically by the directors, "if there is no assistant or deputy secretary or
-- none capable of acting". Name-test sweep of 2026-11-12: two gates. The lead's "Where" is group (i): outside it, JUST FALSE (not
-- flipped). The "if there is no assistant or deputy secretary" is an "if" gate on a function named for a grant: NOTHING (test 1, flipped
-- state; fork F-grants). A thing the secretary was not to do or receive, or a person the directors have not authorised, is outside the
-- grant's own wording and stays NOTHING.
-- src:3618 | Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting, anything required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary may be done—
-- src:3620 | (b) if there is no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable of acting, by or to any person authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors.
@ref s 274(b) Anything required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary: a person authorised by the directors (src:3618-3620)
GIVEN `the office of secretary is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable of acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 274(b) the thing may be done by or to a person authorised by the directors` MEANS
    IF `s 274 the office of secretary is vacant or there is no secretary capable of acting` `the office of secretary is vacant` `there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF       `the thing is required or authorised to be done by or to the secretary`
              AND `there is no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable of acting`
              AND `the person is authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) if there is no assistant or deputy secretary or none capable of acting, by or to any person authorised generally or specifically in that behalf by the directors" (an "if" gate on a grant, name-test sweep test 1; and the thing and the person are outside the grant's own wording)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, group (i), assumed, not ruled): "Where in the case of any company the office of secretary is vacant, or there is for any other reason no secretary capable of acting"; the other reading is NOTHING (F-grants)
